== 5. Gap Analysis: Tradition vs Modern Interpretation
<gap-analysis-tradition-vs-modern-interpretation>
=== 5.1 Where the tradition is correct
<where-the-tradition-is-correct>
- #strong[Lead is dangerous and requires careful processing] —
  accurately observed; the elaborate 60-puta protocol and use of realgar
  in excess reflect serious chemical understanding
- #strong[Sulfurization reduces lead toxicity] — fully validated by
  modern toxicology (PbS dramatically less bioavailable than PbO or
  soluble Pb²⁺)
- #strong[Specific nano-particle PbS form is the proper end-state] —
  accurately observed; modern XRD/TEM confirms 60-85 nm PbS crystallites
- #strong[Lead requires more processing than any other dhatu] —
  accurately observed; 60-puta protocol is the longest in classical
  practice
- #strong[Lead-Shani correspondence (with iron)] — internally coherent
  with both metals’ density and structural properties
- #strong[Lead is excluded from sacred alloys] — accurately observed;
  classical exclusion from panchaloha/ashtadhatu reflects appropriate
  caution
- #strong[Excess realgar ensures complete conversion] — chemically
  validated; the stoichiometry is intentional

=== 5.2 Where the tradition’s claims need qualification
<where-the-traditions-claims-need-qualification>
- #strong["Properly processed naga-bhasma is safe"] — partially true;
  PbS bioavailability is dramatically lower than other lead forms, but
  "lower" is not "zero," and chronic accumulation remains a concern
- #strong[Specific therapeutic claims for diabetes] — under-investigated
  by modern controlled trials; lead toxicity makes such trials ethically
  difficult
- #strong[Long-term safety claims] — #emph[not] supported; chronic lead
  exposure is cumulative regardless of preparation form
- #strong[Use in children] — #emph[contraindicated] by modern medicine
  regardless of classical practice

=== 5.3 Where the framework can help
<where-the-framework-can-help>
- #strong[Identifying when lead operations have lowest graha-pair
  tension] — Shani own-graha nakshatras for sulfurization
- #strong[Predicting which timing windows produce best PbS phase purity]
